    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "gb_calc",
      "spoken": "Now the maths. The Channel Tunnel is 50.5 kilometres long, 38 of them under the sea, says its operator. 164 divided by 50.5 is 3.25. So the bridge is more than three times as long.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "The maths",
        "sheet_dy": 470,
        "calcs": [
          {
